    "filmNote": "Made once in Google Flow (experiments/collections/2026-10-31-next-films, runs/flow/generations.json, rangeelo-film-2): a Nano Banana painting of a pink haveli wall with chhatri balconies, kites and a block-printed cloth rolled below the parapet, an edit of it with the cloth hanging flat, and a Veo 3.1 Fast clip between them in which the roll drops level down the wall like a blind. Veo rolled it back up near the end to meet the edited last frame, so the film is cut at 5.4 s, while it rests with the roll at the foot, and the first and last frames are the film's own (film-1 tilted and twisted the roll and added kites). Cropped to the centred 9:16 window clear of Flow's marks.",
